From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:03:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] posixpath: on AmigaOS defpath is ixemul's
 _PATH_DEFPATH, with C:

With patch 0010 the rig still could not run `which` by bare name:
ixemul's execve() walks only the shell's Path list, and C: (where Which and
the other AmigaDOS commands live) is searched by the shell implicitly, not
from that list. ixemul's own execvp() therefore falls back to
_PATH_DEFPATH "/usr/bin:/bin:/c" when PATH is unset; CPython used
'/bin:/usr/bin'. Use ixemul's value on AmigaOS (os.defpath, the exec
lookup, shutil.which).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XtgdajdQMdzshhCNNkoeFN
---
 Lib/posixpath.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Lib/posixpath.py b/Lib/posixpath.py
index ad86cc0..0695763 100644
--- a/Lib/posixpath.py
+++ b/Lib/posixpath.py
@@ -29,6 +29,13 @@
 import genericpath
 from genericpath import *
 
+if sys.platform == 'amigaos':
+    # ixemul's _PATH_DEFPATH, which its own execvp() walks when PATH is
+    # unset: "/c" is C:, where the AmigaDOS commands live. execve() of a
+    # bare name walks only the shell's Path list, and C: is not on it unless
+    # the Startup-Sequence put it there -- the shell searches C: implicitly.
+    defpath = '/usr/bin:/bin:/c'
+
 __all__ = ["normcase","isabs","join","splitdrive","splitroot","split","splitext",
            "basename","dirname","commonprefix","getsize","getmtime",
            "getatime","getctime","islink","exists","lexists","isdir","isfile",
